    "content": "2026 Best Supporting Actress Winner Veteran actress Amy Madigan won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress in 2026 for her performance in the horror film Weapons. Her victory at the 98th Academy Awards on March 15, 2026, marked her first Oscar win and her first nomination in 40 years. Performance and Awards Season In Weapons, Madigan portrayed Aunt Gladys, an eccentric and menacing figure who is revealed to be a witch. The role became a cultural sensation, noted for its \"scene-stealing\" nature and Madigan's \"creepy\" delivery. Before her Oscar win, Madigan established herself as the frontrunner by winning several major industry awards during the 2026 season: SAG Awards: Won Outstanding Performance by a Female Actor in a Supporting Role. Critics' Choice Awards: Won Best Supporting Actress. New York Film Critics Circle: Named Best Supporting Actress. Historic Milestone Madigan set a new Academy record for the longest gap between an actress's first nomination and her first win, spanning 40 years and one month. Her previous nomination was in the same category for the 1985 film Twice in a Lifetime. 2026 Oscar Nominees Madigan prevailed in a category that experts considered a \"tight race\" without a clear favorite leading into the ceremony. The other nominees were: Teyana Taylor – One Battle After Another Wunmi Mosaku – Sinners Elle Fanning – Sentimental Value Inga Ibsdotter Lilleaas – Sentimental Value",
